---
export const title = 'Collaboration';
export const order = 180;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Several people can edit a document at once. Set <code>collaboration</code>
  to <code>{'{ document, provider, user }'}</code>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>document</code>: a <code>Y.Doc</code> from
    <a href="https://yjs.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Yjs</a>.
    Its fragments <code>body</code>, <code>header</code> and
    <code>footer</code> and its map <code>page</code> hold the document.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>provider</code>: the connection to the others, such as
    <code>y-websocket</code>, Hocuspocus or your own server. Its
    <code>awareness</code> carries each person's caret and name.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>user</code>: the person editing here,
    <code>{'{ name, color?, avatar? }'}</code>.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Edits merge live without conflicts, including the header, footer, page setup
  and comment highlights. Other people's carets show with their names, and
  their avatars appear in the toolbar; <code>presence-change</code> lists who
  is there. Undo only undoes your own edits. Edits from others update
  <code>value</code> without firing <code>input</code>, so save from one place
  (usually the server) rather than from every editor. The first person into an
  empty shared document brings the editor's <code>value</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Install <code>yjs</code> next to Peacock; it is loaded only when
  <code>collaboration</code> is set, and your provider and the editor must use
  the same copy.
</p>

<pre><code>import * as Y from 'yjs';
import {'{ WebsocketProvider }'} from 'y-websocket';

const doc = new Y.Doc();
const provider = new WebsocketProvider('wss://collab.example.com', 'policy-42', doc);
editor.collaboration = {'{'}
  document: doc,
  provider,
  user: {'{'} name: 'Ana Lima', color: '#1a73e8' {'}'},
{'}'};</code></pre>

<p>
  The two editors below are two people on one document, connected in the
  page. Type in either one, change the page setup, or comment, and watch the
  other.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style="display: grid; gap: 16px; width: 100%;">
    <wc-document-editor
      id="collab-ana"
      label="Ana's view"
      style="--document-editor-height: 24rem;"
    ></wc-document-editor>
    <wc-document-editor
      id="collab-ravi"
      label="Ravi's view"
      style="--document-editor-height: 24rem;"
    ></wc-document-editor>
  </div>
  <script is:inline src="/assets/js/mention-demo.js"></script>
  <script type="module" is:inline>
    import { connect } from '/assets/js/collaboration-demo.js';

    const ana = document.getElementById('collab-ana');
    const ravi = document.getElementById('collab-ravi');
    window.peacockMentionDemo(ana);
    window.peacockMentionDemo(ravi);
    await customElements.whenDefined('wc-document-editor');
    await ana.updateComplete;
    ana.importMarkdown(
      '# Launch plan\n\nWe launch the new billing page in **Q1**. Edit this text in either view.',
    );
    await connect(
      [ana, ravi],
      [
        { name: 'Ana Lima', color: '#1a73e8' },
        { name: 'Ravi Kumar', color: '#d93025' },
      ],
    );
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
